<title>CANADA: Imperial Oil lowers posted oil prices.</title>
<headline>Imperial Oil lowers posted oil prices.</headline>
<dateline>CALGARY 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Imperial Oil Ltd said it lowered the price it would pay for Edmonton light sweet crude oil by C$3.00/cubic metre or C$0.48/barrel, to C$174.00/cubic metre or C$27.66/barrel, effective immediately.</p>
<p>Other new prices were listed as follows:</p>
<p>Cromer light sour C$162.00/cubic metre, or C$25.76/barrel</p>
<p>Bow River at Hardisty C$134.00/cubic metre, or C$21.30/barrel</p>
<p>Midale at Cromer C$145.00/cubic metre, or C$23.05/barrel</p>
<p>((Reuters Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624))</p>
</text>
